  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given circuit, the value of current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></math> will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mA</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1425653d-60d7-47c8-9206-b982f09de4cf-image.png\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 115px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a33da0a9-a0a7-4486-93be-1eef8459638c-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 121px;\" /></p><p>Potential drop across the branch containing load resistance will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;due to Zener diode. Therefore, potential drop across&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p>Now, current through battery will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>800</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p><p>Current through load will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>1000</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p>",
